  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7D169CDF6455DFA39F0FB40945B3F193/jobs/90269": {
      "title": "Student Financial Aid Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Financial Aid Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Student Financial Aid Coordinator Waleska, GA 30183 Apply Apply Description Reinhardt University is currently accepting applications for a Student Financial Aid Coordinator in the Student Financial Aid Office. Position Summary: This position is responsible for being the front line of customer service for the Office of Student Financial Aid. Duties include answering incoming Student Financial Aid and Business Office calls & emails, assisting current and prospective students, organizing and filing Financial Aid documents, performing tasks needed for the operation of the office, assisting with the Work Study program, and advising how to make payments and provide student account balance information. Minimum Education & Experience Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree preferred, but would consider work experience in lieu of degree 1-3 years of related work experience Excel experience required Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organization skills Desired Qualifications Include: 1-3 years’ experience in a higher education financial aid environment Hands-on experience with PowerFaids/Jenzabar. Primary Responsibilities/Essential Job Functions: The candidate will be responsible for maintaining student files, processing aid paperwork, responding to Financial Aid and Business Office email and voicemail, and communicating with students and parents in a timely manner. Additional Responsibilities: As appropriate, this position may be required to perform other functions associated with the day-to-day operations or events of the University as assigned by their supervisor. Establish and maintain contacts, processes and procedures with the appropriate departments. (i.e., Business Office, Registrar, Residential Life, Athletics, Faculty and Admissions) The Student Financial Aid Coordinator is an integral component to the success of a student’s college career. Therefore, attendance for this position is generally required at 37.5 hours per week, during normal business hours in person, 8:30 a.m. – 5:00 p.m. As required by seasonal workload, this position may occasionally work overtime. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal, and a clear and effective customer service approach. Demonstrated computer proficiency, especially in the use of excel, and ability to learn new software Demonstrated ability to prioritize work assignments Ability to work hours and events as required Protection of confidentiality of student’s information Work Environment/Physical Requirements of the Job: This position is an in person office environment. The candidate must have the ability to walk between buildings on campus, occasionally lift up to twenty pounds, and be able to work sitting down for long periods of time. Reinhardt University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE/M/V/H/V). Reinhardt University is an equal opportunity institution. The University respects the essential dignity of all individuals and is committed to providing equal access to and support for education and employment opportunities. Reinhardt does not discriminate in any of its policies, programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, age, culture, national origin, socioeconomic status, veteran’s status, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information, religious belief, physical (dis)ability, political affiliation , or any other basis protected by federal, state or local laws. All people involved in the operations of the University are prohibited from engaging in such discrimination. Direct inquiries regarding the equal opportunity and non-discrimination policy to: Director of Human Resources, Reinhardt University, 7300 Reinhardt Circle, Waleska, GA 30183, 770-720-9146. . Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7D169CDF6455DFA39F0FB40945B3F193/jobs/88324": {
      "title": "Instructor of Business",
      "description": "Instructor of Business You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Instructor of Business Waleska, GA 30183 Apply Apply Description REINHARDT UNIVERSITY McCamish School of Business & Professions INSTRUCTOR OF BUSINESS - MARKETING POSITION OVERVIEW Reinhardt University invites applications for the position of Instructor of Business with a focus in Marketing. This is a renewable 9-month faculty appointment in the McCamish School of Business & Professions. The position reports through the academic leadership of the University and is expected to contribute actively to teaching, advising, service, student success, and the continued growth of Reinhardt's business programs. Primary duties include teaching a full course load during the fall and spring terms in on-ground and online formats. Teaching assignments will be based on departmental needs and the candidate's qualifications and may include Principles of Marketing, Digital Marketing, Buyer Behavior, Business Research, Sales Management, Personal Selling, and Marketing Management , as well as other business courses appropriate to the candidate's academic preparation and professional experience. Opportunities may exist to teach additional courses during summer or other terms when enrollment and University needs support additional sections. The successful candidate should demonstrate a commitment to effective collegiate teaching and the use of active, engaged, and applied learning strategies. Particular value will be placed on the ability to connect marketing theory with contemporary professional practice, including digital marketing, consumer insights, sales, market research, analytics, and strategic marketing decision-making. Candidates with meaningful industry experience are especially encouraged to apply, as the program values faculty who can bring current, real-world marketing and business perspectives into the classroom. RESPONSIBILITIES & DUTIES Teach effectively all assigned courses in on-ground and/or online formats during fall and spring terms. Teach undergraduate marketing courses and other business courses consistent with academic credentials and program needs. Develop engaging, applied learning experiences that connect marketing concepts to current business practice. Incorporate appropriate contemporary marketing tools, digital platforms, data, analytics, research methods, and emerging technologies into instruction. Serve as an academic advisor and mentor for business and marketing students, including students exploring majors and career pathways. Assist with assessment of student learning and the development of strategies for continuous program and instructional improvement. Support student retention and success initiatives, including timely outreach to students who may be academically at risk. Participate in program, school, and University meetings and serve on faculty and University-wide committees. Contribute to student recruitment, program promotion, community engagement, and other enrollment-related initiatives. Maintain professional growth within the discipline and remain current with developments in marketing, business, and university teaching. Participate in faculty governance and contribute as an active member of the University community. Follow established University policies, procedures, academic deadlines, and administrative requirements. Perform additional appropriate duties as assigned in support of the mission of the University. IDEAL CANDIDATE WILL DEMONSTRATE Commitment to Reinhardt University's mission of educating the whole person and creating an environment in which students can thrive. Meaningful professional or industry experience in marketing, sales, digital marketing, market research, brand management, business development, or a related field, with the ability to translate that experience into applied student learning. Knowledge of contemporary marketing practice, with the ability to teach across several areas of the marketing curriculum. Strong industry experience and professional accomplishments that can enrich classroom instruction through practical examples, client-based projects, case applications, and career mentoring. Experience or interest in digital marketing, consumer behavior, marketing research, sales, and strategic marketing management. Ability to create an academic environment that values critical thinking, analytical problem solving, effective oral and written communication, collaboration, and intellectual dialogue. Commitment to experiential and applied learning that prepares students to solve authentic business and marketing problems. Ability to integrate appropriate technology and emerging tools into marketing education while emphasizing ethical and responsible professional practice. Commitment to supporting students through academic and career planning and helping them connect their education with professional opportunities. Interest in developing innovative teaching methods that strengthen student learning and engagement in both on-ground and online environments. A collaborative approach to working with faculty colleagues, program coordinators, school leadership, and University administrators in support of enrollment, retention, and program growth. Collegiality, integrity, professionalism, and a strong commitment to student success. QUALIFICATIONS Required: An earned master's degree in marketing, an MBA, or a closely related business field from a regionally accredited institution, with at least 18 graduate semester hours in marketing or another discipline appropriate to the assigned teaching responsibilities. Preferred: Significant professional or industry experience in marketing, sales, digital marketing, market research, brand management, business development, or a related business area is highly valued. Collegiate teaching experience and experience teaching in online or hybrid formats are preferred but not required. Candidates whose professional experience provides substantial applied expertise are encouraged to apply even if their academic background does not align perfectly with the preferred profile, provided they meet applicable University and accreditation requirements for the courses assigned. ABOUT REINHARDT UNIVERSITY Founded in 1883, Reinhardt University is focused on shaping lives and building futures. The University's vision is to create a Reinhardt Experience where each student thrives. Reinhardt's mission is to educate the whole person by developing the intellectual, social, personal, vocational, spiritual, and physical dimensions of its students. As a private comprehensive university grounded in the liberal arts and affiliated with the United Methodist Church, Reinhardt offers undergraduate and graduate programs across a range of academic disciplines. The University is located in Waleska, Georgia, approximately 45 miles north of midtown Atlanta. ABOUT THE MCCAMISH SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & PROFESSIONS The McCamish School of Business & Professions provides undergraduate and graduate education designed to prepare students for professional success, leadership, and continued growth. The successful candidate will join a collegial faculty committed to high-quality teaching, student engagement, applied learning, and service to the University and surrounding communities. APPLICATION INFORMATION Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Application materials and specific submission instructions will be provided through Reinhardt University's employment process. Reinhardt University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE/M/V/H/V). Reinhardt University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC) to award associate, baccalaureate, and master's degrees. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/7D169CDF6455DFA39F0FB40945B3F193/jobs/86230": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Biology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Instructor of Biology Waleska, GA 30183 Apply Apply Description Reinhardt University invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Biology in the College of Humanities, Sciences, and Technology to teach students in Anatomy and Physiology lecture and laboratory during the spring 2027 semester. The position requires a minimum of a master’s degree from a regionally accredited university with 18 graduate hours of credits specific to biology, biomedical science, or a related field, and documented teaching experience. Successful candidates will have shown a dedication to innovative teaching. Duties and responsibilities will include six instructional hours per week, consisting of three-hour lecture courses and/or three-hour laboratory courses in Anatomy and Physiology I and II. Additional responsibilities include grading and maintaining availability to students throughout the semester. Required Qualifications A minimum of a master’s degree from a regionally accredited university with 18 graduate hours of biology, biomedical science, or a related field is required. Apply Applicants must officially apply through the Paycom online application system (click here ) with a cover letter, CV, and contacts for three professional references. Questions about the position can be directed to Dr. Zach Felix, dean of the College of Humanities, Sciences, and Technology at zif@reinhardt.edu. Official graduate transcripts will be requested upon preliminary selection.  Applications are accepted until the position is filled.  Review of applications will start immediately. Reinhardt University Information Founded in 1883, Reinhardt University which values leading, serving, and learning. The University’s vision is to be recognized as a regional university where diverse talents grow.  Reinhardt’s mission is to educate the whole person with challenge and care. As a private comprehensive university grounded in the liberal arts and affiliated with the United Methodist Church, Reinhardt offers 40+ graduate and undergraduate programs, ranging from biology, business and education to music, theatre, and creative writing. Reinhardt is located in Waleska, Georgia, 45 miles north of mid-town Atlanta. Reinhardt University is accredited by the Commission on Colleges of the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools (SACSCOC) to award associates, baccalaureate and master's degrees. Contact the Commission on Colleges at 1866 Southern Lane, Decatur, Georgia 30033-4097 or call 404-679-4500 for questions about the accreditation of Reinhardt University. Reinhardt University is an equal opportunity institution. The University respects the essential dignity of all individuals and is committed to providing equal access to and support for education and employment opportunities. Reinhardt does not discriminate in any of its policies, programs, or activities on the basis of race, color, age, culture, national origin, socioeconomic status, veteran’s status, gender, sexual orientation, genetic information, religious belief, physical (dis)ability, political affiliation , or any other basis protected by federal, state or local laws. All persons involved in the operations of the University are prohibited from engaging in such discrimination. Direct inquiries regarding the equal opportunity and non-discrimination policy to: Director of Human Resources, Reinhardt University, 7300 Reinhardt Circle, Waleska, GA 30183, 770-720-5897. Reinhardt University is an Equal Opportunity Employer (EOE/M/V/H/V). Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
